## Allowed origins

The Worker's CORS config in `worker/src/index.ts` (mounted globally via `app.use('*', cors({...}))`) allows:
- `http://localhost:4200` (exact match)
- any origin ending in `.pages.dev`
- any origin ending in `.workers.dev`

## Where to add a new custom domain

Edit the `origin` function passed to `cors()` in **`worker/src/index.ts`** (documented in `worker/src/index.md` and `docs/DEPLOYMENT_NOTES.md §4 CORS`):

```typescript
app.use('*', cors({
  origin: (origin) => {
    if (!origin) return null;
    if (
      origin === 'http://localhost:4200' ||
      origin.endsWith('.pages.dev') ||
      origin.endsWith('.workers.dev')
    ) {
      return origin;
    }
    return null;
  },
  ...
}));
```

Add your new domain as another `origin === '...'` check (or an `.endsWith('.yourdomain.com')` check for subdomains) inside this condition. Note: Hono's `cors()` requires `origin` as a **function**, not a string array, because wildcard/subdomain matches (`*.pages.dev`, `*.workers.dev`) don't work as literal array entries.
